# Consultancy Pro (Q Engineering): Cursor Rules (summary)

The detailed rules live in `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`, and Cursor loads them automatically:
- `00-project-core.mdc` (always): app, stack, Railway deploy target, secrets, commands, working style
- `10-database-migrations.mdc` (backend/database/**, backend/scripts/**): new migration files only, RLS, audit fields, constraints
- `20-frontend.mdc` (frontend/web/**): feature-folder pattern, limsThemeUi, supabase client, forms
- `30-railway-functions.mdc` (backend/services/functions/**, backend/services/gateway/**): production QI Assistant = qiAssistant.mjs
- `40-knowledge-engine.mdc` (knowledge_engine/**): usable/needs_review gate, protected collections, same embedding model, evals
- `50-workflow-prompts.mdc` (always): docs/audits/*.md with VDB-xx / MST-xx / FIN-xx IDs, "continue" workflow
- `60-extensions.mdc` (frontend/extensions/**): keep the Chrome and Safari copies in sync

If `.cursor/rules` isn't loaded, follow this short version:

## AI behaviour
- Search the codebase first, then edit. Edit files directly; don't dump long code blocks in chat.
- Apply multi-file changes together. Keep changes small and reviewable, and don't touch unrelated files.
- After changes run `npm run lint` and `npm run typecheck` (frontend), `node --check` (railway functions), and the `knowledge_engine.scripts.test_*` modules (Python). End with a summary of files changed and verification.
- Don't commit or push unless asked.

## Project structure
- `frontend/web/`: React 19 + Vite 7 + TypeScript, shadcn/ui, LIMS stone/amber theme (`lib/limsThemeUi.ts`)
- `frontend/extensions/`: Chrome and Safari extension
- `backend/database/migrations/`: Railway Postgres SQL (new files only, never edit applied ones, RLS on every table). Not Supabase.com.
- `backend/services/gateway/`: Caddy API gateway. `backend/services/functions/`: Node functions (users, Resend email, QI Assistant)
- `backend/services/pdf-service/`: Playwright PDF. `backend/services/storage-minio/`: legacy MinIO Dockerfile
- `knowledge_engine/`: local BIS RAG (Python), standalone; HTTP only

Paths moved on 2026-10-08, see `docs/REPO_STRUCTURE.md`. If a prompt uses an old path (`frontend/src`, `railway-stack/...`, `pdf-service/`, `storage-service/`, `extensions/`, `scripts/apply-migrations.mjs`, `scripts/dump-schema.mjs`, `scripts/gen-db-types.mjs`, `backend/supabase/...` including `backend/supabase/migrations` and `backend/supabase/schema`), map it to the new path automatically (`backend/supabase/` → `backend/database/`). `backend/supabase/functions` was deleted (recover from git at `4e28cc0`).

## Rules
- Railway self-hosted stack only. Never use hosted Supabase Cloud, `supabase db push`, Vercel or Netlify. Don't deploy unless asked.
- Never read, print or commit `.env*` or `.railway-secrets.env`.
- UI/theme: reuse the existing `limsThemeUi` and MasterPage patterns.
- App UI is in English (EN/हिंदी toggle only where a page already has one). Explanations in Hindi/Hinglish are fine.
- Write "Quality International Research & Laboratories Private Limited" in full, never "Pvt Ltd".
- Domain: BIS ops, clients, IS codes, finance, email.
- Audits and plans live in `docs/audits/`. On "continue" or an item ID: implement it, verify, then update its status in the file.
